  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 805.02 Expiration of Sludge Hauler Permits",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 805.02 Expiration of Sludge Hauler Permits. Any sludge hauler permit issued pursuant to this part shall be valid for up to 2 years according to the following schedule:\n\n(a) Permits issued in an even numbered year will expire on January 31 of the next even numbered year following the date of issuance; and\n\n(b) Permits issued in an odd numbered year will expire on January 31 of the next odd numbered year following the date of issuance.\n\nSource. #10998, eff 1-1-16; ss by #14571, eff 5-15-26, EXPIRES: 5-15-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq800.html"
}
